  "question": "In a patient with a history of heart transplantation and a pacemaker, presenting with two nodular shadows in the right lung observed on routine chest X-ray, which of the following is the most likely diagnosis for the nodular lesions, considering the absence of symptoms and geographic exposure?\n\nA) Post-transplant lymphoproliferative disorder\nB) Lung tumor (primary or secondary)\nC) Pulmonary blastomycosis\nD) Histoplasmosis\nE) Tuberculosis\nF) Fungal infection other than blastomycosis",
